    /*
   * The bars are geometry, not a mask.
   *
   * This used to knock them out with `<mask id="wave">`, which works right up
   * until the same logo renders twice on one page: two elements then share the
   * id, every `url(#wave)` resolves to whichever comes first in the document,
   * and if that one happens to sit in a `display:none` subtree it contributes
   * no geometry and the knock-outs quietly stop happening. The tile fills
   * solid and only the accent bar survives, which is exactly what /demo did
   * once it started rendering the deck and the grid at the same time and
   * hiding one of them.
   *
   * An even-odd fill needs no id, so it cannot collide however many times it
   * renders or which copy is visible. Same five bars, same rounded tile.
   */
